2026-07-27T09:52Z HDMX-coding-agent note ADD TO THE MONDAY RECONCILIATION LIST — the letter quotes a number that is now wrong. response-letter.md:154-155 and summary-of-revisions.md:29 and citation-quality-response.md:31 all state the Crossref audit as '99.0% confirmed, 95% CI [97.1%, 99.7%]'. Those are corpus-v1 figures; on the frozen v2 corpus qa_citations_report.json gives 97.0%, CI [94.4%, 98.4%], 9 unconfirmed of 300. The claimed point estimate falls outside the current interval. The paper itself is fixed and vars-driven in PR #1131 (ticket 0320); the letter is not, and it is the document the editor reads. Also worth adding to the letter: the completeness test (98.3% of Crossref-held reference DOIs captured, CI [98.0, 98.6]) which strengthens the R1-13 answer and was never quoted.
